#: ../../docs/jobs/index.rst:3 4eaa9ad19ae44482b51c2daf2e56f8c4
msgid "作业系统"
msgstr "Job System"

#: ../../docs/jobs/index.rst:5 37a35a69eee6489e93bde94ae611b6fb
msgid ""
"cnSRC通过Slurm调度系统进行资源和作业管理，提高运行效率，以此来完成程序的规范运行，最新文档参考 "
"[Slurm官网](https://slurm.schedmd.com/documentation.html)。"
msgstr ""
"cnSRC uses the Slurm scheduler for resource and job management to improve "
"efficiency and ensure programs run in a standard way. For the latest "
"documentation, see the [Slurm "
"website](https://slurm.schedmd.com/documentation.html)."

#: ../../docs/jobs/index.rst:7 a3529879ab014615b6988b1795c5e1dd
msgid ""
"所有需要运行的作业，无论是程序调试还是业务计算，都必须通过交互式并行srun、批量提交sbatch或分布式salloc命令提交，提交后可以使用相关命令查询作业状态。"
msgstr ""
"All jobs that need to be run, whether it is program debugging or business "
"calculation, must be submitted through the interactive parallel srun, batch "
"submission sbatch or distributed salloc command. After submission, you can "
"use the relevant command to query the job status."

#: ../../docs/jobs/index.rst:11 55e1940cc7854426bdd30f319a2d9bb6
msgid "本章节介绍了作业系统的基本使用方法，如果你是第一次接触作业系统，建议你先阅读 :ref:`slurm_intro` 章节。"
msgstr ""
"This chapter introduces the basic usage of the job system. If you are new to"
" the job system, it is recommended that you read the :ref:`slurm_intro` "
"chapter first."

#: ../../docs/jobs/index.rst:13 6dedc59ade6b401b914827f8510ce225
msgid ""
"如果你顺利完成了上面的步骤，那么是否可以直接让服务器运行你的程序了呢？ "
"答案是不可以的，如果你在登录后直接运行程序，很抱歉，会被终止掉，这是因为登录节点是不允许运行程序的， 你需要使用作业调度系统 SLURM "
"来运行你的程序。 如果你留意登录之后显示的主机名，名为 workstation 的主机仅仅为用户提供了登录操作的平台， "
"但程序的运行需要交给它背后的计算节点们完成。那么如何告诉工作站来运行我们的程序？ 我们需要使用作业调度系统SLURM，它给我们提供了若干运行程序的方式，"
" 在本章节里我们简要介绍最常用的方式：提交 SLURM 作业脚本的批处理方式。"
msgstr ""
"If you have completed the steps above, can you run your program on the "
"server directly? No. If you run a program immediately after logging in, it "
"will be terminated—login nodes must not run compute workloads. You need the "
"SLURM job scheduler to run your program. If you notice the hostname shown "
"after login, the host named ``workstation`` only provides a platform for "
"login operations; actual execution is handled by compute nodes behind it. To"
" run your program, use SLURM, which offers several ways to launch jobs. This"
" chapter briefly introduces the most common approach: batch submission via "
"SLURM job scripts."

#: ../../docs/jobs/index.rst:22 5c897b8d5afb48ec9bab6dbae76561e7
msgid "请不要在登录节点上直接运行作业，以免影响其他用户的正常使用。"
msgstr ""
"Please do not run jobs directly on the login node to avoid affecting the "
"normal use of other users."

#~ msgid "首先需要编写一个 SLURM 脚本。"
#~ msgstr "First, you need to create an SLURM script."

#~ msgid "准备好 SLURM 脚本之后，使用"
#~ msgstr "After preparing the SLURM script, use the following steps"

#~ msgid "$ sbatch run.slurm"
#~ msgstr "$ sbatch run.slurm"
